.TH brother-td 7 "2026-11-17" "brother-td-cups 1.0.0" "Driver Manual"
.SH NAME
brother-td \- CUPS driver for Brother TD-4D label printers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lpadmin
.RB \-p " queue"
.B \-E
.BI \-v " device-uri"
.BI \-m " brother-td-4410d.ppd"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brother-td-cups
is a CUPS driver for Brother TD-4D series direct-thermal label printers.
It consists of the
.BR brother-td-filter (7)
CUPS raster filter and a PPD for each supported model.
.PP
The driver converts CUPS raster pages to the printer's native raster command
stream. It works with the standard CUPS
.BR usb ,
.BR socket ,
and other backends; no proprietary backend is required.
.SH SUPPORTED MODELS
The following models have PPDs:
.PP
.nf
TD-4210D   TD-4410D   TD-4420DN   TD-4510D   TD-4520DN   TD-4550DNWB
TD-4215D   TD-4415D   TD-4425DN   TD-4455DNWB TD-4525DN  TD-4555DNWB
TD-4425DNF TD-4555DNWBF TD-4420DNFC TD-4550DNWBFC
.fi
.PP
203 dpi models have an 832-pin head; 300 dpi models have a 1280-pin head.
.SH INSTALLATION
Build and install the driver:
.PP
.nf
make
sudo make install
.fi
.PP
Find the device URI:
.PP
.nf
lpinfo -v | grep -i brother
.fi
.PP
Create a queue:
.PP
.nf
sudo lpadmin \-p TD4410 \-E \\
    \-v 'usb://Brother/TD-4410D?serial=000G0G123456' \\
    \-m brother-td-4410d.ppd
sudo lpadmin \-d TD4410
.fi
.PP
For a network model, use a raw socket URI such as
.BR socket://192.168.1.50:9100 .
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be selected in the CUPS web interface or passed with
.BR "lp \-o name=value" .
.TP
.B PageSize
Physical label or page size. Common values are
.BR 102x152mm ,
.BR 102x102mm ,
.BR 102x50mm ,
.BR 76x26mm ,
and
.BR 51x26mm .
Custom sizes are supported.
.TP
.B TDMediaType
.B DieCut
or
.BR Continuous .
The default is
.BR DieCut .
.TP
.B Resolution
.B 203dpi
or
.BR 300dpi ,
fixed by the model PPD.
.TP
.B ColorModel
Only
.B Gray
is available. It requests 8-bit grayscale CUPS raster so the driver
controls halftoning.
.TP
.B TDModel
Optional explicit model name. When omitted, the filter infers the 203/300 dpi
head from the raster and uses the safe 661-byte invalidate sequence.
.TP
.B TDDither
.BR Floyd ,
.BR Jarvis ,
.BR Stucki ,
.BR Atkinson ,
.BR Sierra ,
.BR SierraLite ,
.BR Burkes ,
.BR Bayer4 ,
.BR Bayer8 ,
or
.BR Threshold .
The default is
.BR Floyd .
.TP
.B TDThreshold
Threshold value (64, 96, 128, 160, or 192). The default is 128.
.TP
.B TDScaling
.BR Fit " (shrink only),"
.BR FitEnlarge ,
.BR Crop ,
or
.BR None .
The default is
.BR Fit .
.TP
.B TDRotate
.BR 0 ,
.BR 90 ,
.BR 180 ,
or
.BR 270 .
.TP
.B TDInvert
Invert black and white.
.TP
.B TDMirror
Mirror the image horizontally.
.TP
.B TDBorder
Print the non-imageable side margins black.
.TP
.B TDAlignX
.BR Left ,
.BR Center ,
or
.BR Right .
.TP
.B TDAlignY
.BR Top ,
.BR Center ,
or
.BR Bottom .
.TP
.B TDMargin
Feed margin in millimetres for continuous media. The default is 3 mm.
Ignored for die-cut labels.
.TP
.B TDAutoTrim
Trim blank leading and trailing rows on continuous media. The default is
.BR True .
.TP
.B TDAutoCut
Enable the auto-cutter on continuous media. The default is
.BR False .
.TP
.B TDCutAtEnd
Cut at the end of the job. The default is
.BR True .
.TP
.B TDPeeler
Enable the peeler on continuous media. The default is
.BR False .
.TP
.B TDCompression
.B TIFF
(PackBits) or
.BR None .
The default is
.BR TIFF .
.SH EXAMPLES
Print a 4 x 6 inch die-cut label:
.PP
.nf
lp \-d TD4410 \-o PageSize=102x152mm \-o TDMediaType=DieCut label.pdf
.fi
.PP
Print on a continuous roll with a 10 mm feed margin:
.PP
.nf
lp \-d TD4410 \-o PageSize=102x100mm \-o TDMediaType=Continuous \\
   \-o TDAutoTrim=True \-o TDMargin=10 label.pdf
.fi
.PP
Print three copies:
.PP
.nf
lp \-d TD4410 \-n 3 label.pdf
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/cups/filter/brother-td-filter
The CUPS raster filter (path from
.BR cups-config\ \-\-serverbin ).
.TP
.I /usr/share/cups/model/brother-td-*.ppd
The generated PPD files.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Enable CUPS debug logging with
.BR "cupsctl \-\-debug\-logging" ,
then inspect
.IR /var/log/cups/error_log .
Set
.B BROTHER_TD_DEBUG=1
in the CUPS environment for filter diagnostics, and
.B BROTHER_TD_DEBUG_DIR
to a directory writable by the filter user to capture the raw printer stream
as
.IR job-\fIid\fB.prn .
.PP
Run
.B make check
in the source tree to validate the filter, PPDs, and protocol encoding without
a printer.
